From: cube oakley <cube-oakley@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 01:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: simple: accept a sensor configuration within 1% of
 the processed stream size

The simple pipeline picks the smallest sensor configuration whose largest
processed output covers the requested stream. The software ISP's debayer
leaves an 8-column margin, so a binned mode exactly as wide as the request
never covers it, and the full-resolution mode wins instead, at four times
the data.

A configuration that falls short by at most 1% in each direction now
qualifies too, and the stream is adjusted down to it. On the Pixel 7 Pro
the front camera's 1080p video moves from the 3840x2736 mode to the
1920x1368 binned one (1912x1080 out), and the software ISP's time per frame
halves; every other camera and role keeps its mode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -1235,12 +1235,23 @@
 	const SimpleCameraData::Configuration *maxPipeConfig = nullptr;
 	pipeConfig_ = nullptr;
 
+	/*
+	 * A sensor configuration whose largest output falls short of the
+	 * processed stream by at most 1% in each direction also qualifies; the
+	 * stream is then adjusted down to it. A converter may need a margin
+	 * (the software ISP's debayer leaves 8 columns), so an otherwise
+	 * matching binned mode would lose to a full-resolution one it cannot
+	 * process at the same frame rate: 1912 of 1920 columns, for example.
+	 */
+	const Size nearProcessedStreamSize{ maxProcessedStreamSize.width * 99 / 100,
+					    maxProcessedStreamSize.height * 99 / 100 };
+
 	for (const SimpleCameraData::Configuration *pipeConfig : *configs) {
 		const Size &captureSize = pipeConfig->captureSize;
 		const Size &maxOutputSize = pipeConfig->outputSizes.max;
 
-		if (maxOutputSize.width >= maxProcessedStreamSize.width &&
-		    maxOutputSize.height >= maxProcessedStreamSize.height &&
+		if (maxOutputSize.width >= nearProcessedStreamSize.width &&
+		    maxOutputSize.height >= nearProcessedStreamSize.height &&
 		    captureSize.width >= maxRawStreamSize.width &&
 		    captureSize.height >= maxRawStreamSize.height) {
 			if (!pipeConfig_ || captureSize < pipeConfig_->captureSize)
